# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored by the existing `.env*.local` rule).
#
# The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is what makes a variable visible to app code. Expo
# CLI replaces every literal `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_NAME` in your source with
# the value at bundle time.
#
# ============================  READ THIS  ============================
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ values are embedded in the shipped app IN PLAIN TEXT. Anyone who
# installs the app can read them, so NOTHING SECRET MAY GO HERE.
#
# An API's address is fine: it is configuration, and anyone can see it by
# watching one request. A credential is not. An earlier version of this app put
# a bearer token here, which meant every install shipped the same readable key,
# it could not be revoked without an app update, and every user shared one
# account. Credentials now come from signing in - the device sends an email and
# password to POST /auth/signin and gets back a short-lived access token plus a
# refresh token it keeps in the OS keychain. See part 9 of
# docs/CLOUDFLARE_R2_EXPO_GUIDE.md.
# =====================================================================

# Leave UNSET during local development: the app then derives the Worker's
# address from the Metro dev server's own host, which is the one address your
# phone, simulator and emulator can all reach. Set it to point at a deployed
# Worker, or at a tunnel.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_PHOTO_VAULT_API_URL=https://photo-vault-api.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev
